# Root build context exclusions.
#
# frontend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile.railway both build from the
# REPOSITORY ROOT, because frontend/ has no package-lock.json of its own —
# dependencies are an npm workspace hoisted to the root lockfile. Without this
# file the "few MB" context the frontend Dockerfile assumes is a lie: model/ is
# ~943 MB, and a dev machine's node_modules adds another few hundred. That is
# uploaded to the builder on every deploy, on Docker Desktop and on Railway
# alike.
#
# The only things a frontend build needs are the two manifests, frontend/ and
# shared/. Everything else is excluded below.
#
# backend/ is excluded too: it has its own Dockerfile and its own
# backend/.dockerignore, and its build context is backend/, never the root.

# --- VCS / editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# --- Python service and its tests (separate build context) ------------------
backend
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage

# --- Training data, notebooks and exported artifacts ------------------------
# 943 MB of datasets, notebooks and runs. Nothing in the SPA bundle reads it.
model

# --- SQL fixtures, screenshots, local scripting -----------------------------
database
docs
scripts
locustfile.py

# --- Node installs and build residue ---------------------------------------
# The image runs `npm ci` itself; a host node_modules is the wrong platform and
# would be copied over the freshly installed one.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
**/.vite
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
npm-debug.log*

# --- Compose / docs not needed in a build context ---------------------------
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
Makefile
*.md
!frontend/*.md
